[interviewer · CLARIFY · 1:45] Okay. I'll take your store question as a data request and come back to it. Before I do, which part of that structure would you prioritize first, and why?

[candidate · 3:15] I'd prioritize the cost side, and specifically the cost structure as a percent of revenue, then and now.

The reason is the magnitude. Margin dropped eighteen points — veinticuatro a seis — while revenue grew. If revenue is up and profit is way down in absolute terms, something on the cost side has to have moved a lot, and probably a single big line, not five small ones drifting.

Let me just sanity-check that with numbers. Say revenue two years ago was 100, so profit was 24 and costs were 76. Now revenue is 115, margin 6%, entonces profit is 115 por 0.06, que son 6.9. So costs are 115 menos 6.9, about 108. Costs went from 76 to 108 — that's up roughly 42%, against revenue up 15%.

So costs are growing almost three times as fast as revenue. That's where I'd start.

Do we have a cost breakdown by major line item for both periods?
